- Home/End in zsh (B). Measured cause: shell/bashrc bound the keys and *then*
  ran `bindkey -e`, which links a fresh emacs keymap over `main` and discards
  whatever was bound into the previous one. Machine-dependent, which is why it
  worked on moose: zsh starts in viins when $EDITOR contains "vi", so a host
  without helix lost the bindings and a host with it kept them. The keymap is
  now chosen above the bindings, and ^[OH / ^[OF (application cursor mode,
  which zle's own smkx asks the terminal for) are bound as well.
  tests/test_shell_keys.py.

- `wk sysimage ls` carries a STATE column: building | ready | none, from the
  workspace's own live answer. An image being built is the one most likely
  being looked for and `-` in the size column was not an answer.
  tests/test_card_edits.py.

- Default CMake flags for every config, and per-machine flags per config
  (`WK_TARGET_CMAKE_<config>`, `WK_BUILD_ARGS_<config>` in a machine's conf).
  Each config now states only what differs from the default. tests/test_build.py.

- `wk pr <ref>` no longer refuses a pull request as a missing workspace. The
  declaration gained `takes=<n>`: how many positionals belong to the command
  after the name, so a lone one is the command's. An audit test holds every
  command with an optional name to it.

- On a shared build box the *directory* now names the workspace: `cd
  ~/wk/ws/<name> && wk build gtk-release` works, as it does inside a container
  workspace. There is no workspace marker on those machines -- several live
  side by side under one root -- which is why the in-workspace interface only
  ever worked in a container. tests/test_dispatcher.py.

- git identity and speed settings reach every machine, from the one file that
  declares them (dotfiles/gitconfig) rather than a copy per machine:
  container/firstrun.sh and remote/provision.sh include it, `./setup` removes a
  [user] section that shadows it (git takes a key's *last* value, so an include
  loses to anything written after it), and `wk doctor` checks all three.
  Found by it: devbox-arm64-2 has `user.name = no` and `user.email = no`, so
  every commit made there is authored by "no <no>"; buildbox4 has no identity
  at all, so a commit there is refused after the work. Both fixed by re-running
  `wk remote setup <target>`.

- `wk doctor --all` asks every build machine what it has, read-only over ssh:
  the tools a build needs, the identity a commit there would carry, and any
  build variable that machine's own profile sets. One list of prerequisites
  (remote/deps.sh) answers for `wk remote setup`, provisioning and doctor, and
  whatever is missing comes back as one exact root command -- provisioning
  still never takes root. tests/test_remote_deps.py.
  Found by it: buildbox4 has no ccache, so every build there starts cold.

- A machine's own environment is no longer overwritten: shell/bashrc keeps a
  pre-set $EDITOR/$VISUAL, and `wk doctor --all` prints any CC/CXX/CCACHE_DIR
